Eudaimonia: not merely happiness, but human flourishing—living so that your abilities, character, relationships, and actions become fully alive and well-ordered.

Pleasure is a feeling. Success is an outcome. Eudaimonia is a way of being across an entire life.

In Pantheon terms:

\text{Eudaimonia}
=
\text{Virtue}
\times
\text{Capability}
\times
\text{Meaningful Action}
\times
\text{Relational Belonging}
\times
\text{Time}

It is thrive, not merely survive—but with virtue governing what “thrive” means. The good life is not something you possess; it is something you continually enact.